/-! # Excellent blowups and projective closed transforms

Source: Stacks Project, Divisors, Tags 0804, 02ND and 02NS; More on Algebra,
Tag 07QU; Morphisms, Tags 01QR, 01QS and 01T6
(blueprint: lem-trf-excellent-blowup-projective-transforms).

The symmetric quotient is characterized on all symmetric monomials, including
empty products. Its induced relative-Proj morphism is the specified immersion.
The two projectivity conclusions use their distinct recorded conventions.
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option relaxedAutoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory Limits Opposite

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData

/-- Blowups in finite-type ideals, trivial on a nonempty open of an excellent integral
Noetherian scheme, are excellent integral Noetherian proper birational schemes, with
the canonical closed immersion into P(I); closed subschemes of base-changed
H-projective schemes remain H-projective. Standard charts have the stated fraction rings.

Source: Stacks Project, Divisors, Tags 0804, 02ND and 02NS; More on Algebra,
Tag 07QU; Morphisms, Tags 01QR, 01QS and 01T6
(blueprint: lem-trf-excellent-blowup-projective-transforms).

Proof:
1. The ideal is nonzero since it is the unit ideal on the nonempty open U of the
   integral base. Apply lem-sfb-integral-blowup-chart-density: nonzero generators
   give domain chart rings A[I/a] inside A_a, zero generators give empty charts,
   and the center complement W is nonempty and dense. The injective localization
   map A_a to Frac(A) embeds the same chart rings in Frac(A).
2. thm-nagata-global-blowup-complement identifies the inverse image of W with W.
   It meets every nonempty chart densely, so is dense in the blowup. The domain
   charts make the blowup reduced; its dense nonempty irreducible open makes it
   irreducible, hence integral by def-pc-integral-scheme. These dense opens give
   birationality. lemma-nagata-blowup-proper gives properness, and
   lem-weil-pbc-finite-type-over-noetherian gives Noetherianity.
3. Use lem-trf-excellent-scheme-affine-cover on an excellent affine cover of S.
   Each chart A[I/a] is generated by the finite list of generator fractions, hence
   is a finite-type A-algebra. lem-exc-finite-type-localization-excellent makes it
   excellent. The affine-cover criterion gives excellence of every affine of T.
4. lem-sfb-sheaf-rees-symmetric-presentation gives the canonical degreewise
   multiplication surjection Sym(I) to Rees(I), fixing degree zero. Apply
   lem-sfb-rees-presentation-blowup-immersion: the canonical relProjReesIso
   identifies the ordinary blowup with relative Proj of its Rees algebra, and the
   induced Proj map is a closed immersion over S. Taking E = I in
   def-trf-projective-bundle-morphism gives projective-bundle projectivity.
5. Choose the finite projective-space embedding of X from def-kun-projective.
   Base-change it along T to S, using lem-weil-pbc-closed-immersion-base-change
   and lemma-nagata-projective-space-base-change-pullback. Compose with the
   given closed immersion of Y, using lem-weil-pbc-closed-immersion-comp.
   This is an embedding of Y into the same finite projective space over T.
   Neither flatness nor nonemptiness of Y is needed. -/
theorem excellent_blowup_projective_transforms
    {S : Scheme.{u}} [IsIntegral S] [IsNoetherian S]
    (hexc : ∀ V : S.affineOpens, IsExcellent Γ(S, V.1))
    (I : S.IdealSheafData) (hfinite : I.toModules.IsQuasiCoherentFiniteType)
    (U : S.Opens) (hU : Nonempty U)
    (hunit : Disjoint (U : Set S) (I.support : Set S)) :
    (∀ V : I.blowup.affineOpens, IsExcellent Γ(I.blowup, V.1)) ∧
    IsIntegral I.blowup ∧ IsNoetherian I.blowup ∧ IsProper I.blowupMap ∧
    IsIso (I.blowupMap ∣_ I.support.compl) ∧
    Dense (I.support.compl : Set S) ∧
    Dense (I.blowupMap ⁻¹ᵁ I.support.compl : Set I.blowup) ∧
    (∃ hqc : I.toModules.IsQuasicoherent,
      ∃ q : (@SymmetricAlgebraSheaf.gradedAlgebraData S I.toModules hqc ⟶ I.reesData),
        (∀ (V : S.affineOpens) (n : ℕ), Function.Surjective ((q.app V).gradedAddHom n)) ∧
        (∀ (V : S.affineOpens) (n : ℕ) (x : Fin n → Γ(I.toModules, V.1)),
          (reesAlgebra (I.ideal V)).subtype
            (q.app V (∏ i, SymmetricAlgebra.ι Γ(S, V.1)
              (I.toModules.val.obj (op V.1)) (x i))) =
            Polynomial.monomial n (∏ i, @id Γ(S, V.1) (I.toModulesι.app V.1 (x i)))) ∧
        ∃ hq : GradedAlgebraData.IrrelevantLE q,
          IsClosedImmersion (I.relProjReesIso.inv ≫ GradedAlgebraData.relProjMap q hq) ∧
          (I.relProjReesIso.inv ≫ GradedAlgebraData.relProjMap q hq) ≫
            (@SymmetricAlgebraSheaf.gradedAlgebraData S I.toModules hqc).relProjHom =
              I.blowupMap) ∧
    IsProjectiveBundle I.blowupMap ∧
    (∀ (X : Scheme.{u}) (f : X ⟶ S), IsHProjective f →
      ∀ (Y : Scheme.{u}) (i : Y ⟶ pullback f I.blowupMap), IsClosedImmersion i →
        IsHProjective (i ≫ pullback.snd f I.blowupMap)) ∧
    (∀ (V : S.affineOpens) (r : ℕ) (a : Fin r → I.ideal V),
      Ideal.span (Set.range (fun j ↦ (a j : Γ(S, V.1)))) = I.ideal V →
        (⨆ j, Proj.basicOpen (reesGrading (I.ideal V))
          (reesX (I.ideal V) (a j).1 (a j).2)) = ⊤ ∧
        ∀ j : Fin r,
          ((a j).1 = 0 → IsEmpty (Proj.basicOpen (reesGrading (I.ideal V))
            (reesX (I.ideal V) (a j).1 (a j).2))) ∧
          ((a j).1 ≠ 0 →
            IsDomain (AffineBlowup.chartRing (I.ideal V) (a j).1) ∧
            (∃ e : (Proj.basicOpen (reesGrading (I.ideal V))
                (reesX (I.ideal V) (a j).1 (a j).2)).toScheme ≅
                  Spec (.of (AffineBlowup.chartRing (I.ideal V) (a j).1)),
              e.hom = (Proj.basicOpenIsoSpec (reesGrading (I.ideal V))
                (reesX (I.ideal V) (a j).1 (a j).2)
                (reesX_mem (I.ideal V) (a j).1 (a j).2) one_pos).hom ≫
                  Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom
                    (AffineBlowup.homogeneousAwayEquivChart (I.ideal V) (a j).2).symm.toRingHom) ∧
              e.inv ≫ (Proj.basicOpen (reesGrading (I.ideal V))
                  (reesX (I.ideal V) (a j).1 (a j).2)).ι ≫ I.blowupι V =
                Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom
                    (AffineBlowup.homogeneousAwayToChart (I.ideal V) (a j).2)) ≫
                  Proj.awayι (reesGrading (I.ideal V))
                    (reesX (I.ideal V) (a j).1 (a j).2)
                    (reesX_mem (I.ideal V) (a j).1 (a j).2) one_pos ≫ I.blowupι V) ∧
            ∃ ρ : Localization.Away (a j).1 →ₐ[Γ(S, V.1)] FractionRing Γ(S, V.1),
              Function.Injective ρ)) := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData
